## Opt-in use, explicit fallback

From this research worktree, select a **new root** for each attempt. Do not restart the already-used C188 root. C143 rejects inherited LLAMA/TESY/GGML/CUDA/LD overrides; clear them explicitly if present.

```sh
TESY_SESSION=results/local-optin-slots40-$(date -u +%Y%m%dT%H%M%SZ)
python3 tools/c143_slots40_optin.py prepare --root "$TESY_SESSION" --profile slots40 --port 18440 --duration-s 900
python3 tools/c143_slots40_optin.py command --root "$TESY_SESSION"
python3 tools/c143_slots40_optin.py start --root "$TESY_SESSION"
curl --fail http://127.0.0.1:18440/health
# Send OpenAI-compatible HTTP chat requests with medium, seed42/temp0,
# the fixed preset date and the actual assistant history.
python3 tools/c143_slots40_optin.py stop --root "$TESY_SESSION"
```

Start waits for another60s per-arm inventory before model Popen; /health must become ready. Full argv, date and hashes in preset, command output and launch receipt. Local-only900s bounded session, not permanent activation. Prefix persistence only inside same model/process/profile/date/KV; restart persistence NOT_RUN. For explicit C35 fallback, stop slots40 first, choose another new root, run prepare with `--profile c35`; follow command/start/health/stop. No automatic fallback or KV transfer.

